ed crash logging remains functional, including after restart. The restart protocol otherwise showed a healthy baseline, acknowledged restart, independently confirmed boot-ID change, and recovered system and service health.","limitations":["Only the daemon account was behavior-tested; coverage of other local service accounts follows from the global effective coredump policy rather than individual tests.","The pre-restart crash journal query returned no record after restart, so persistence of historical crash-log entries across reboot was not demonstrated. This weakens restart-data evidence but does not negate the successful fresh post-restart logging test.","The fixed lifecycle snapshots confirm the boot-ID transition and healthy host state but do not independently inspect the coredump configuration file."]}
